lesson: 128
title: Cuts, posts and floors: the gaps between
level: primary-1
stars: 2
explain: To cut a log into 4 pieces you need only 3 cuts: the last piece needs no cut. Between 4 posts in a row there are only 3 gaps.
explain: So count the gaps, one fewer than the pieces or posts. 5 posts 2 m apart: 4 gaps, 2 + 2 + 2 + 2 = 8 m from the first post to the last.
explain: Walking from the 1st floor to the 4th you climb only 3 flights of stairs.
vars: a=name k=3..10 m=2..5
answer: (k - 1) * m
exercise: {a} saws a log into {k} pieces. Each cut takes {m} minutes. How many minutes does {a.he} need?
exercise: {k} posts stand in a straight line, {m} metres apart. How far is it from the first post to the last, in metres?
exercise: There are {k} trees in a row with {m} metres between neighbouring trees. How many metres is it from the first tree to the last tree?
exercise: Between two floors of a house there are {m} steps. {a} walks from the 1st floor up to the {k.ord} floor. How many steps does {a.he} climb?
exercise: A ribbon is cut into {k} pieces. Every cut takes {m} seconds. How many seconds does the cutting take?
test: {a} lives on the {k.ordwords} floor. Each flight of stairs between floors has {m} steps. How many steps does {a.he} climb from the first floor to {a.his} home?
test: A clock strikes {k} times. There are {m} seconds between one strike and the next. How many seconds pass from the first strike to the last?
test: {k} children stand in a line, each {m} steps from the next. How many steps is it from the first child to the last?
test: To cut a long bar into {k} equal parts, a worker needs {m} minutes for every cut. How long does the job take, in minutes?
exercise: {a} cuts a log into {k} pieces, and every cut takes {m} minutes. How long does all the sawing take, in minutes?
exercise: Along a road in Kansas, {k} fence posts stand in a line, each {m} yards from the next. What is the distance from the first post to the last, in yards?
exercise: {k} oak trees grow in a row in an English park, {m} metres apart. How many metres is it from the first oak to the last?
exercise: In an apartment building in Chicago there are {m} steps between one floor and the next. How many steps does {a} climb going from the 1st floor to the {k.ord} floor?
exercise: A piece of ribbon is snipped into {k} bits. Each snip takes {m} seconds. How many seconds does the snipping take?
exercise: How long does it take to cut a pipe into {k} parts if each cut takes {m} minutes?
exercise: {k} lamp posts line a street in Sydney, with {m} metres between neighbouring posts. How far apart are the first and last posts, in metres?
exercise: A long loaf is cut across into {k.words} pieces. Each cut takes {m} seconds. How many seconds does it take to cut the loaf?
test: {a}'s flat is on the {k.ord} floor of a building in New York. Each flight between two floors has {m} steps. From the 1st floor, how many steps does {a.he} climb to get home?
test: A church bell in Dublin rings {k} times, with {m} seconds between rings. How many seconds are there from the first ring to the last?
test: {k} pupils line up in a Toronto schoolyard, {m} steps from one to the next. How many steps separate the first pupil from the last?
test: A plumber in Melbourne cuts a pipe into {k} equal lengths. Every cut takes {m} minutes. How many minutes does the job take?
test: There are {k} flags along a race track, with {m} metres between each flag and the next. What distance is there between the first and last flags, in metres?
test: A carpenter needs {m} minutes for each cut. She saws a plank into {k} pieces. How many minutes does she work?
