exam: It is given that a log is to be divided by sawing into {k} pieces and that each cut occupies {m} minutes. Determine the total duration, in minutes, of the sawing.
exam: Whereas {k} posts are erected in a straight line at intervals of {m} metres, ascertain the distance, in metres, between the first post and the last.
exam: A row consists of {k} trees, adjacent trees being separated by {m} metres. State the distance, in metres, from the first tree to the last.
exam: Compute the total time required, in minutes, for {a} to divide a plank into {k} pieces, each cut requiring {m} minutes.
exercise: The old tree in Grandad's garden "gave up the ghost", so {a} saws it into {k} pieces. Each cut takes {m} minutes. How many minutes does {a.he} need?
exercise: Granny is "getting on a bit", so a hand rail goes by her path on {k} posts in a straight line, {m} metres apart. How long is the rail from the first post to the last, in metres?
